  ('saas-fee-switzerland', '01F', 'Saas-Fee', 'Switzerland', 'The Pearl of the Alps', 'live', 'verified', 'northernLights', 'Switzerland & the Alps', '{"ski","adventure","family","wellness","culinary","ultra","romance"}', '{}', '{"essential","comfort","premier","luxury","ultra"}', null, 'emerging', '{"key_facts":["Car-free village since 1951 (park at entrance; electric buggies only) — the ''Pearl of the Alps'', Saas Valley, Valais, ~1,800 m","Ringed by thirteen 4,000-m peaks (Dom, Allalinhorn, Weissmies, Nadelhorn, Lenzspitze) — densest cluster in the Alps (official site markets 38 regional — flagged)","Ski area on the Feegletscher/Allalin glacier: ~100 km pistes (Wikipedia cites 150 km — flagged), ~20/60/20 easy/intermediate/difficult, ~22-23 lifts, base 1,800 m to ~3,500 m Mittelallalin (summit ~3,573 m)","Metro Alpin = highest underground funicular in the world (to Mittelallalin ~3,500 m); Allalin = highest revolving restaurant in the world","Glacier + SUMMER skiing on the Allalin (national-team summer training base); operating window ~mid-Jul to late Apr","Adult day pass ~CHF 83 (youth ~71 / child ~42, via skiresort.info — verify live + Metro Alpin surcharge); Magic Pass member; no Ikon/Epic","SaastalCard on arrival = free valley cable cars + PostBus (Metro Alpin excluded)","Car-free arrival: SBB rail to Visp (or Brig) + PostBus line 511 Visp->Saas-Fee every 30 min","Luxury base: The Capra Saas-Fee (boutique 5-star) + Ferienart Resort & Spa (ratings/spa detail to verify)","Haute Route glacier ski-touring runs from the Saas valleys; thirteen 4,000-m peaks give guided summer mountaineering from the village","Glacier descent ~1,773 m vertical from Mittelallalin (~3,500 m) to the village (~1,800 m); ~60% intermediate terrain = progression/family-friendly","Two-season rhythm: winter + spring skiing, summer break for lower runs, Allalin glacier reopens in high summer","Sits east of Zermatt in the same Valais high country — the quiet glacier village to Zermatt''s Matte