  ('schladming-austria', '01F', 'Schladming', 'Austria', 'Four linked mountains, up to 760 km on one', 'live', 'verified', 'northernLights', 'Austria', '{"ski","entertainment","family","adventure","wellness","nightlife","culinary"}', '{}', '{"essential","comfort","premier","ultra"}', null, 'emerging', '{"key_facts":["4-Berge-Skischaukel = Planai + Hochwurzen + Hauser Kaibling + Reiteralm, ~185 km piste (65.5 easy / 104.6 medium / 11.6 diff), 109 lift installations (brief''s ''123 km'' = legacy/marketing - use 185)","Ski amadé pass = up to ~760 km (356 pistes) across 25 places in 5 regions, ~270 lifts (Schladming-Dachstein is one member region)","Planai Nightrace = FIS World Cup night slalom (Planai a WC venue since 1973, night races since 1997); January; draws tens of thousands - the season''s wildest night","Hosted the FIS Alpine World Championships 2013 (and 1982)","Dachstein Glacier (Hoher Dachstein 2,995 m) nearby via Ramsau = year-round skiing + Skywalk/suspension bridge","Elevations ~728-2,015 m (Hauser Kaibling top ~2,015 m; Planai summit 1,894 m, base ~750 m); mid-altitude, heavy snowmaking (~90% coverage)","Village ~745 m, Styria (Steiermark), Liezen District, upper Ennstal; former mining town (~6,660 residents)","Reached by rail on the Ennstalbahn (Schladming''s own station; Bischofshofen-Selzthal) from Salzburg/Graz; airports Salzburg + Graz","Ski amadé pass standalone; no confirmed Ikon/Epic affiliation","Heli-skiing NOT available (Austria permits it only at Vorarlberg/Lech-Zurs sites)","Avalanche = Lawinenwarndienst STEIERMARK (Land Steiermark) via lawinen.report, EAWS 5-level - NOT SLF/Meteo, NOT Tirol/Vorarlberg","Wellness is hotel-spa-based; the public Erlebnistherme Amade is in Altenmarkt (Salzburg), NOT Schladming","Dense 4-star (+ some higher) hotel base, expanded for the 2013 Worlds (ratings to verify)","Nearest hospital = Schladming / Stainach-Rottenmann (LKH) area (verify)","A four-season town: winter 4-Berge + Nightrace, year-round Dachstein g