  ('tignes-france', '01F', 'Tignes', 'France', 'Ski into July on a 3,600-metre glacier', 'live', 'verified', 'northernLights', 'French Alps', '{"ski","family","hiking","wellness","ultra","entertainment"}', '{}', '{"essential","comfort","premier","luxury","ultra"}', null, 'emerging', '{"key_facts":["Grande Motte glacier summit 3,656 m; funicular to 3,032 m + cable car to 3,456 m (~7 min); ~20 km of glacier runs 3,456-2,724 m","Espace Killy / Tignes-Val d''Isere: 300 km pistes, 80 lifts, 1,550-3,456 m, 154 runs (22 green/61 blue/46 red/25 black)","One of the longest seasons in Europe: 2025/26 winter 22 Nov 2025 (glacier) / 29 Nov link - 3 May 2026; glacier autumn training","Summer skiing on the Grande Motte glacier ~20 Jun-15 Jul 2026 (snow-dependent); summer day pass ~EUR 49","High-altitude villages: Les Brevieres 1,550 m -> Le Lavachet 2,050 m -> Tignes le Lac 2,100 m -> Val Claret ~2,150 m","Adult day lift pass ~EUR 48-71; pass free for children under 8; free Lagon pool with 2-10 day pass","Freeride/off-piste + DC Park snowpark (DC Shoes); Winter Fest 10-13 Jan 2026; Evolution2 Freeride Series (reg to 5 Feb 2026)","Summer: 25-hectare lake watersports, 55 km marked trails, ~230 km bike park (28 Jun-31 Aug), altitude training (Tignespace) at 2,100 m; Vanoise National Park (1963, France''s first) at the gateway","Maison Bouvier (Les Suites) - first 5-star in resort, 24 suites (from ~EUR 410 B&B), URSUS restaurant by chef Clement Bouvier"],"safety":{"emergency":"112 (Europe/English) / 15 SAMU medical / 17 police / 18 fire-pompiers / 114 SMS; mountain rescue via 112 (PGHM)","hospital":"Centre Medical de Tignes (in-resort urgent care); Centre Hospitalier de Bourg-Saint-Maurice (~17 km); trauma transfer Chambery/Grenoble, often by helicopter","advisory_level":"L2","malaria":"none","yellow_fever":"not required","activity_note":"High-alpine winter sports: off-piste avalanche risk (Meteo-France BERA bulletin, European 5-level scale; transceiver/shovel/probe + guide), glacier