ture","tier":"essential","price_band":"~EUR 40-100/pp (approx)","timing":"~Jun-Sep, snow-free","draw_rank":2,"hook":"a two-hour hike from the Manchet valley to the Fond des Fours refuge","si":"Hiking & Outdoor","blurb":"a two-hour hike from the Manchet valley to the Fond des Fours refuge","when":"~Jun-Sep, snow-free","commission":"operator/bundle"},{"name":"A guided Grand Paradis / Vanoise nature trek","si_tag":"Hiking & Outdoor","status":"future","tier":"comfort","price_band":"~EUR 90-200/pp/day (approx)","timing":"~Jun-Sep","draw_rank":3,"hook":"multi-day guided trekking from Val d''Isère into the Vanoise — ibex, marmots, glaciers and refuges, the deep-nature version of the summer season","si":"Hiking & Outdoor","blurb":"multi-day guided trekking from Val d''Isère into the Vanoise — ibex, marmots, glaciers and refuges, the deep-nature version of the summer season","when":"~Jun-Sep","commission":"operator 10-15%"}],"faq":[{"q":"Where is the nearest hospital to Val d''Isere?","a":"The nearest hospital is the Centre Hospitalier de Bourg-Saint-Maurice Tarentaise, about 25 km / 40 minutes away, with a 24/7 emergency department, SMUR and trauma surgery. Major trauma is routed through the Alpine network to the Level-1 trauma centre at CHU Grenoble Alpes, with CHU Chambery the other regional referral. The emergency number is 112. (Source: https://www.ch-bsm.fr/urgences.html and https://www.chu-grenoble.fr/patients-et-accompagnants/offre-de-soin/urgences-adultes-nord - accessed 2026-08-06.)","source":"https://www.ch-bsm.fr/urgences.html","si_tag":"safety"},{"q":"When is the best time to ski Val d''Isere?","a":"The core winter season runs late November to early May - the official 2026-27 dates are 28 November 2026 to 2 May 2027 - plus a summer glacier season on the Pissaillas roughly early July to late August. High terrain (village 1,850 m, lifts to about 3,197 m on the Pissaillas glacier and about 3,456 m area-wide at the Grande Motte) makes snow relatively reliable, but exact opening and closing shift with conditions. (Source: https://www.valdisere.com/en/val-disere/faq/ and https://www.seevaldisere.com/lifts/dates - accessed 2026-08-06; verify before travel.)","source":"https://www.valdisere.com/en/val-disere/faq/","si_tag":"ski"},{"q":"How much is a Val d''Isere lift pass?","a":"For winter 2025-26 the Tignes-Val d''Isere full-area adult pass is about EUR 75 for one day and EUR 450 for six days (ages 19-64); it is cheaper early and late season and is effectively dynamic by date. 2026-27 prices were not published as of August 2026. (Source: https://www.seevaldisere.com/ski-passes/ and https://www.valdisere.com/en/prepare-for-your-stay/buy-my-skipass/ - accessed 2026-08-06; verify before travel.)","source":"https://www.seevaldisere.com/ski-passes/","si_tag":"ski"},{"q":"Is Val d''Isere good for beginners?","a":"For progression yes, with a caveat: the linked Tignes-Val d''Isere area is about 300 km of piste with green and blue runs and ski schools, but much of Val d''Isere''s own terrain is red and black and the village home runs can be demanding, so beginners are usually pointed to the La Daille and Solaise nursery areas. (Source: https://www.valdisere.com/en/val-disere/faq/ - the ''I am a beginner, where should I go to ski?'' entry - accessed 2026-08-06.)","source":"https://www.valdisere.com/en/val-disere/faq/","si_tag":"ski"},{"q":"Val d''Isere or Tignes - which, and how do I get there?","a":"They share one 300 km linked ski area (historically l''Espace Killy, now marketed as Tignes-Val d''Isere) on a single pass, so the choice is base-village character rather than terrain. Nearest airports are Geneva, Lyon and Chambery with a roughly 2.5-3.5 hour transfer; the nearest railway station is Bourg-Saint-Maurice, about 30 km away, with an onward bus or transfer. (Source: https://www.valdisere.com/en/val-disere/faq/ and https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tignes_%E2%80%93_Val_d%27Isere - accessed 2026-08-06.)","source":"https://www.valdisere.com/en/val-disere/faq/","si_tag":"ski"}],"seo":{"meta_title":"Val d''Isere Travel Guide: Snow-Sure Skiing, the Espace Killy & World Cup Racing","meta_description":"Plan Val d''Isere — the snow-sure Tarentaise resort at 1,850 m: the 300 km Espace Killy linked with Tignes, the Olympic Face de Bellevarde and Criterium de la Premiere Neige World Cup, legendary off-piste, snow-front five-star palaces and the Vanoise National Park, with real timing, safety and booking intel.","slug":"val-d-isere-france","primary_keyword":"Val d''Isere travel guide","long_tail":["Val d''Isere ski season dates","Espace Killy Tignes Val d''Isere piste map","Face de Bellevarde","Criterium de la Premiere Neige World Cup","Val d''Isere off-piste","Val d''Isere luxury hotels"],"search_language":"fr","local_keywords":["Val d''Isere guide de voyage","domaine skiable Espace Killy Tignes","Face de Bellevarde","Criterium de la Premiere Neige","hors-piste Val d''Isere","hotels de luxe Val d''Isere","Parc national de la Vanoise"],"hreflang":["en","fr-FR"],"jsonld_type":"TouristDestination","author_byline":"By David McCallister — commercial pilot, 56 countries","content_freshness":"2026-07-17"},"booking":{"bin":"freely_bookable","level":"L2 (Exercise Increased Caution)","codes":["terrorism","civil-unrest","petty-crime"],"advisory_updated":"2026 (L2 reaffirmed; accessed 2026-07-17)","consent_flow":false,"note":"France is US L2 (not a warning against travel); concerns are urban terrorism/protests/pickpocketing — in-resort the main risk is the alpine environment, not security"},"si_checklist_25":null,"sis_present":[{"si":"ski","status":"live"},{"si":"adventure","status":"future"},{"si":"Sports Travel","status":"future"},{"si":"Luxury / Ultra-Luxury","status":"future"},{"si":"Apres-ski & Nightlife","status":"future"},{"si":"romance","status":"live"},{"si":"wellness","status":"future"},{"si":"Hiking & Outdoor","status":"future"}],"ultra":[{"name":"Airelles Val d''Isere","why_ultra":"snow-front Airelles five-s