  ('verbier-switzerland', '01F', 'Verbier', 'Switzerland', 'Switzerland''s freeride capital', 'live', 'verified', 'northernLights', 'Switzerland & the Alps', '{"ski","adventure","ultra","culture","wellness","romance"}', '{}', '{"essential","comfort","premier","luxury","ultra"}', null, 'core', '{"key_facts":["Les 4 Vallees (Verbier, Bruson, La Tzoumaz, Nendaz, Veysonnaz, Thyon) = Switzerland''s largest linked ski area: 412 km pistes, 68 lifts, 1,350-3,330 m","Piste breakdown: ~107 km easy (26%), 202 km intermediate (49%), 103 km difficult (25%); Verbier home sector ~106 km / 33 lifts","Mont-Fort 3,330 m — highest lift-served point; classic backside off-piste ~1,830 m vertical, starts 35-40 degrees","Xtreme Verbier / Freeride World Tour finale on the Bec des Rosses (3,223 m, 607 m vertical, 43 degrees) since 1996; 30th ed. ran 28 Mar 2026","2025/26 ski season 6 Dec 2025-26 Apr 2026; 4 Vallees adult day pass CHF 94 (youth 80 / child 47)","Village at 1,500 m in French-speaking Valais; reached via Le Chable (train + 10-min gondola), ~2-3 hrs from Geneva","W Verbier (1,531 m) — only 5-star ski-in/ski-out in resort, 123 rooms, 1,300 sqm spa; Le Chalet d''Adrien (Relais & Chateaux, 29 rooms, 1 Michelin star)","Nightlife: ~12 bars/clubs led by Farinet apres, Pub Mont Fort, Farm Club (since 1970s)","Verbier Festival (classical music) 33rd ed. 16 Jul-2 Aug 2026, 60+ concerts, ~100 masterclasses, tickets CHF 30-220","Patrouille des Glaciers ski-mountaineering race (biennial): 2026 ran 13-19 April; Zermatt-Verbier route 57.5 km / 4,386 m climb"],"safety":{"emergency":"112 / 117 police / 118 fire / 144 ambulance / 1414 REGA alpine air-rescue / 145 poison","hospital":"Hopital de Martigny (~20 min); Hopital de Sion regional referral centre; local Verbier medical centre; REGA 1414 alpine evac","advisory_level":"L1","malaria":"none","yellow_fever":"not required","activity_note":"Serious off-piste/freeride mecca — avalanche is the killer: SLF five-level bulletin (slf.ch), transceiver/